{:en {:title "Kotoba native performance: Embench progress, 12 October 2026"
:description "Resumed work: Round 84 gives Kotoba 2.877× C execution time across all 19 workloads. Small validated improvements are adopted; the C-or-faster goal remains unmet."
:intro "Work resumed on 12 October 2026. The latest complete 19-workload comparison gives Kotoba execution time / C of 2.877× in geometric mean. C is faster overall and the C-or-faster goal remains unmet. The earlier Round 83 result and dated pause are retained below as history."
:notice "These are exploratory measurements of translated Kotoba programs using the upstream Embench speed driver and formula. They are not a certified official Kotoba Embench score, a released-toolchain result, or a claim of speed on other hosts."
:sections [{:title "Resumed work — verified Round 84"
:paragraphs ["Work resumed after the paused snapshot below. Its Round 83 table and dated pause history are retained; they do not describe the resumed compiler or Round 84. The C-or-faster goal remains unmet."
"A generic bounded byte lookup replaces eligible pure scalar threshold trees while preserving full 64-bit inputs, original fuel, traps and workload. Original qualification covered 39 native images and 483 comparisons; the current main composition reproduced all 39 qualified images byte for byte."
"Four fixed OFF/ON samples per workload observed 2.0851% shorter PicoJPEG time and 0.7699% shorter QRduino time. These exploratory two-pair observations have no uncertainty estimate and are not a combined or total-suite gain. There is no minimum 5% improvement cutoff; correctness and regression checks still apply."
"Main PR #1293 merged as 9bdff08f95effda253a08b2eed190efe98af55fc; remote main ancestry, source and native-image bindings were verified. Independently verified Round 84 accepted all 19 Kotoba and all 19 fresh C measurements across 41 retained attempts. Normalized Kotoba time / C was 2.876720502080424 (2.877×); C remained faster overall. Driver geometric scores were 12916.907866571351 for translated Kotoba and 37158.333683249715 for original C. This single exploratory cycle does not establish a statistical improvement over Round 83. Translated Kotoba measurements remain exploratory and are not certified official Embench scores."]}
